NAME
       bal asyncapi - Generate Ballerina sources from AsyncAPI definitions or
       export AsyncAPI from Ballerina services.

SYNOPSIS
       bal asyncapi [-i | --input] <path> [-o | --output <directory>]
                    [--protocol <http|https|ws|wss|websocket>]
                    [--license <license-file>]
                    [--service <service-name>]
                    [--json]
                    [--with-tests]

DESCRIPTION
       By default this command reads an AsyncAPI definition and generates an
       HTTP listener skeleton. The following Ballerina files are produced in the
       output directory:
        1. `data_types.bal` - Contains the data types derived from the AsyncAPI
            contract
        2. `service_types.bal` - Contains service type definitions required by
            the listener
        3. `listener.bal` - Contains the HTTP listener that interacts with the
            event source
        4. `dispatcher_service.bal` - Contains the event dispatching logic

       When --protocol is set to `ws`, `wss`, or `websocket`, the tool targets
       WebSocket services. Supplying an AsyncAPI contract (YAML or JSON)
       generates a WebSocket client package, optionally with tests and a license
       header. Supplying a Ballerina service (.bal) exports the AsyncAPI
       definition in YAML or JSON form.


OPTIONS
        -i, --input <path>
            Path to the source file. Provide an AsyncAPI contract to generate
            Ballerina sources, or a Ballerina service (.bal) when exporting an
            AsyncAPI definition for WebSocket services.

        -o, --output <directory>
            Directory to store generated files. Defaults to the current
            execution directory.

        --protocol <http|https|ws|wss|websocket>
            Protocol to target. Defaults to `http`. Use `ws`, `wss`, or
            `websocket` to work with WebSocket tooling.

        --license <license-file>
            Path to a text file whose contents are prepended as the license
            header in generated WebSocket client sources. Valid only when
            generating from an AsyncAPI contract for WebSocket services.

        --service <service-name>
            Name of the Ballerina service to document when exporting an AsyncAPI
            definition. Applicable only when converting a WebSocket Ballerina
            service.

        --json
            Export the AsyncAPI definition in JSON format instead of YAML when
            converting a WebSocket Ballerina service.

        --with-tests
            Generate basic test files alongside the WebSocket client sources.
            Applicable only when generating from an AsyncAPI contract for
            WebSocket services.


EXAMPLES
       Generate an HTTP listener from an AsyncAPI contract.
           $ bal asyncapi -i slack-events.yaml

       Generate a WebSocket client with tests and a license header.
           $ bal asyncapi -i websocket-api.yaml --protocol ws -o ./ws-client \
             --with-tests --license ./license.txt

       Export an AsyncAPI definition in JSON for a specific WebSocket service.
           $ bal asyncapi -i websocket-service.bal --protocol ws --service \
             ChatService --json -o ./specs
